title: First-ever Podemos party congress
subtitle: Party members from all of Spain meet in Madrid to decide the party's structure
view-if: podemos_vista_alegre_one_trigger
role: event
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/events/vistaalegre0.webp
on-arrival: {!
    // Compare population-weighted valid-vote shares across contests.
    var ally = Q.parlament_current_icv || 'icv';
    var valid = 0, allied = 0, cup = 0;
    for (var c of Q.parlament_constituencies) {
        for (var d of Q.parlament_demographics) {
            var weight = Q['parlament_' + c + '_' + d + '_pop'] || 0;
            for (var p of Q.parties) {
                if (p == 'abstain') continue;
                var votes = weight * (Q[p + '_parlament_' + c + '_' + d + '_support'] || 0);
                valid += votes;
                if (p == ally) allied += votes;
                if (p == 'cup') cup += votes;
            }
        }
    }
    var congresoValid = Q.congreso_parties_catalunya.reduce((sum, p) => sum + (Q[p + '_congreso_catalunya_support'] || 0), 0);
    var nationalLeft = (Q.podemos_congreso_catalunya_support || 0) + (Q.up_congreso_catalunya_support || 0);
    var congresoShare = congresoValid > 0 ? 100 * nationalLeft / congresoValid : 0;
    var allyShare = valid > 0 ? 100 * allied / valid : 0;
    var cupShare = valid > 0 ? 100 * cup / valid : 0;
    var localValid = Q.parties_bcn.reduce((sum, p) => sum + (Q[p + '_local_barcelona_support'] || 0), 0);
    var localLeft = (Q.icv_local_barcelona_support || 0) + (Q.bcomu_local_barcelona_support || 0);
    var localShare = localValid > 0 ? 100 * localLeft / localValid : 0;
    // Provisional: autonomous allies retain 60% of the national umbrella's
    // appeal, or a CUP player demonstrates credible assembly-based strength.
    Q.podemos_autonomy_credible = allyShare >= Math.max(5, congresoShare * 0.6)
        || localShare >= Math.max(5, congresoShare * 0.6)
        || (Q.player_party == 'cup' && cupShare >= Math.max(5, congresoShare * 0.4));
    Q.podemos_relations_required = Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55;
    Q.podemos_player_access = Q.player_party == 'erc' || Q.player_party == 'cup';
    Q.podemos_relations_ok = Q[ally + '_relations'] >= Q.podemos_relations_required;
!}

= First-ever ​Podemos party congress

While the Pablo Iglesias has been, by far, the most visible leadership of this new political organization, the internal structure of the newly-born party is still quite unclear. So far, the preferred organization of the movement has been through "circles", local assemblies with varying degrees of autonomy and professionalization. It is, however, unclear what level of independence these will retain as the party formalizes its structure.

On one side of the debate, Pablo Iglesias himself, and his number two, Íñigo Errejón, defend a centralized party able to operate coherently as a single force, betting on that unity as a driver for electoral success. On the flip side, Teresa Rodríguez and Pablo Echenique demand that the original idea of the "circles" is enshrined. Local parties operating semi-independently, with a confederal party organization able to leverage and organize its grassroots power.

The party congress in Vistalegre is going to be the final decision moment before the upcoming Spanish general election, and will be defining the party moving forward.

- @one
- @many

@one
title: Podemos becomes a centralized party
subtitle: Pablo Iglesias will have it his way.
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.podemos_vista_alegre_one_trigger) {
        Q.podemos_vista_alegre_one_trigger = false;
        G.setText(Q, 'podemos_ideology', G.text('Anti-austerity Left, Plurinationalism'));
        for (var c of Q.congreso_constituencies) {
            if (c == 'rest') G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'podemos', c, 0.75, 'abstain');
            else G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'abstain', c, 0.75, 'podemos');
        }
        Q.podemos_vista_alegre_two_countdown = 28;
        if (!Q.countdowns.includes('podemos_vista_alegre_two')) Q.countdowns.push('podemos_vista_alegre_two');
    }
!}

Unsurprisingly it the remarkable media presence and undoubted leadership of Pablo Iglesias has tipped the scales in his favour. Podemos now begins the process of party formation not so dissimilar to their ancestors.

- @post_event: Another lost opportunity, and more of the same for the Spanish left...

@many
title: The "circles" remain the main power holders
subtitle: We'd have to push some social advocacy groups out of their comfort zone to make this even a possibility. \[-1 resources\]
choose-if: {! return Q.podemos_autonomy_credible && Q.party_resources >= 1 && (Q.player_party == 'erc' || Q.player_party == 'cup') && Q[Q.parlament_current_icv + '_relations'] >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55); !}
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not podemos_autonomy_credible: [+ parlament_current_icv +] lacks electoral weight for this challenge to work. ?][? if not podemos_player_access: We don't have any avenue to influence this decision.. ?][? if not podemos_relations_ok: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_icv +]. ?][? if party_resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.podemos_vista_alegre_one_trigger && Q.podemos_autonomy_credible && Q.party_resources >= 1
        && (Q.player_party == 'erc' || Q.player_party == 'cup')
        && Q[Q.parlament_current_icv + '_relations'] >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55)) {
        Q.party_resources -= 1;
        Q.podemos_vista_alegre_one_trigger = false;
        G.setText(Q, 'podemos_ideology', G.text('Anti-austerity Left, Confederalism'));
        for (var party of ['bng', 'compromis', 'mes']) {
            Q['party_reaching_out_' + party] = Math.max(-2, (Q['party_reaching_out_' + party] || 0) - 1);
        }
        for (var c of Q.congreso_constituencies) {
            if (c == 'rest') G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'abstain', c, 0.75, 'podemos');
            else G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'podemos', c, 0.75, 'abstain');
        }
        Q.podemos_vista_alegre_two_countdown = 28;
        if (!Q.countdowns.includes('podemos_vista_alegre_two')) Q.countdowns.push('podemos_vista_alegre_two');
    }
!}

The unpredictable seems to have happened: the factions spearheaded by Teresa Rodríguez and Pablo Echenique have been able to out-vote the centralization proposals, and Podemos will instead start its party structure build-up as a confederal association, with heavy internal weights favouring local assemblies and grassroots participation. 

- @post_event: We'll have to see if this really is a new chance for the Spanish left...
